WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.950
A family tree with no faces.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:07.970
At the root, a Puritan in a tall
hat, with a Bible and a sword.

3
00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:13.400
Further up, an open court
record, and a date: 1692.

4
00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:17.660
At the top, two centuries
on, a descendant with a pen.

5
00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:22.890
His ancestors, he imagines, would
scoff: "A writer of story-books!"

6
00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:26.650
A page blows back to a
wooden town with a scaffold.

7
00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:30.460
So how does that family
past shape his Boston?

8
00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:35.170
In this mission, you'll meet the real
people of 1640s Boston who walk through

9
00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:36.060
the novel.

10
00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:39.770
You'll find out why the colony
is called a theocracy in spirit.

11
00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:43.670
And you'll read what the narrator
says about his own ancestors.

12
00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:48.280
Your mission: explain how that
family past shapes his Boston.
